{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-139526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ Given that the eigenvalues of ${A}^{T}A$ are $15,$ $10,$ and $0,$ find the length of the ellipse's semi-major axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto the ellipse ${Ax\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, let's re-write the squared distance from the origin to the point $Ax$ on our ellipse, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Ax{‖}^{2} & =(Ax)^{T}(Ax) \\\\  & =({x}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})(Ax) \\\\  & ={x}^{T}\\,({A}^{T}\\,A)x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere ${x}^{T}({A}^{T}A)x$ is the quadratic form with the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$ \n\nThe maximum value of this quadratic form, when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$\n\nSince the largest eigenvalue of ${A}^{T}A$ is $15,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax{‖}^{2}}=15\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax‖}=\\sqrt{15}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is $\\sqrt{15}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13159d7d5c6860406c5296d68a4d24ed916db843734f36548e75b4a55bbef43c"} {"question" "q-139526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{15}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ Given that the eigenvalues of ${A}^{T}A$ are $12,$ $9,$ and $0,$ find the length of the ellipse's semi-major axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto the ellipse ${Ax\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, let's re-write the squared distance from the origin to the point $Ax$ on our ellipse, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Ax{‖}^{2} & =(Ax)^{T}(Ax) \\\\  & =({x}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})(Ax) \\\\  & ={x}^{T}\\,({A}^{T}\\,A)x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere ${x}^{T}({A}^{T}A)x$ is the quadratic form with the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$ \n\nThe maximum value of this quadratic form, when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$\n\nSince the largest eigenvalue of ${A}^{T}A$ is $12,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax{‖}^{2}}=12\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax‖}=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is $2\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13159d7d5c6860406c5296d68a4d24ed916db843734f36548e75b4a55bbef43c"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathaca