mbda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}={5}^{2}.$ So, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax{‖}^{2}}={5}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax‖}=5.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is ${\\sigma }_{1}=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13159d7d5c6860406c5296d68a4d24ed916db843734f36548e75b4a55bbef43c"} {"question" "q-139541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/state.json" "file_sha256" "8db308feb568fa0c1c2b6c0d11e8647c4baf266f2cbe17415f677e15d5c71807"} {"question" "q-139543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖